  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A wire carrying current <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math> is bent in the shape<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ABCDEFA</mi></math> as shown, where rectangle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ABCDA</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ADEFA</mi></math> are perpendicular to each other. If the sides of the rectangles are of lengths <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi></math>, then the magnitude and direction of magnetic moment of the loop&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ABCDEFA</mi></math> is :</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0167_90831fe3da09.png\" style=\"width: 341px; height: 262px;\" /></p>"
